{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b632dfaf3723bb76","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-B-E002\n3\ttitle: External vector store connection management with validated connectivity\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9007\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: B\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9007-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9007-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: remove\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the platform-managed posture is selected, per-project external\n16\t    connection registration is not delivered; this epic is removed in favor of the\n17\t    operator-managed deployment path.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: 0\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 6\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\t---\n34\t# External vector store connection management with validated connectivity\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tThis epic delivers the core of the external-connection-only posture: data\n39\tscientists can register an external vector store connection per project, with\n40\tconnectivity validated as part of registration, and manage those connections\n41\tthrough the Dashboard. Registration (with validation) and the connection\n42\tmanagement UI are one capability on one surface for the Dashboard component\n43\tand team, so they are delivered together in this epic rather than split.\n44\t\n45\t## Scope\n46\t\n47\t- Implement per-project registration of an external vector store connection\n48\t  covering the connection details a vector store requires (endpoint and\n49\t  credentials), stored as a project-scoped resource.\n50\t- Validate connectivity to the external vector store as part of registration,\n51\t  so a connection is only accepted when it actually reaches the store.\n52\t- Provide the Dashboard connection management UI for external vector store\n53\t  connections: list, create, edit, and remove connections within a project.\n54\t- Keep connection credentials handled per the platform's existing secret\n55\t  handling conventions — no new credential storage mechanism.\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- A data scientist can register an external vector store connection scoped to\n60\t  a project.\n61\t- Registration validates connectivity to the external vector store; a\n62\t  connection that cannot be reached is rejected with a meaningful error.\n63\t- The Dashboard lists, creates, edits, and removes external vector store\n64\t  connections within a project.\n65\t- Connection credentials are not exposed in plaintext in the UI or in\n66\t  connection listings.\n67\t\n68\t## HLR Traceability\n69\t\n70\t- HLR-2 (P0, external path): data scientists can register an external vector\n71\t  store connection per project with validated connectivity.\n72\t- HLR-4 (P1, external path): the Dashboard exposes connection management UI\n73\t  for the external path — the same surface as HLR-2's registration\n74\t  capability, covered by this epic rather than split out.\n75\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-af45a68bd2a7fec1","agent_id":"a8029498acbc7c540","session_id":"456aa445-a015-4ed6-b66f-fb5c63ab7c74","uuid":"bfef24fc-ff51-4fc4-9cc2-72dbdf576b64","timestamp":"2026-10-22T17:52:40.106Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b632dfaf3723bb76","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9007 decomposition"}
