ure alternative — true gates, not scheduling dependencies.\n104\tImplementation epics all produce concrete artifacts. Implementation-type\n105\tlabels are consistent (general implementations carry null\n106\timplementation_type).\n107\t\n108\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (1/2)\n109\tType-appropriate signal sets are used throughout (investigation_signals\n110\ton E001, ai_signals on all Implementation epics) and all 11 ai-signals\n111\trationale files exist with values matching frontmatter. E001's signals\n112\tmatch the rubric closely — `source_accessibility: 0` is exactly the\n113\trubric's \"answer doesn't exist yet\" condition for an undecided posture,\n114\tand `human_judgment_required: -2` correctly captures that the gating\n115\tquestion is a product decision. Two arguable values on BRANCH-A-E005:\n116\t(a) `existing_foundation: 0` — the epic extends the existing Platform\n117\tOperator codebase (its own `pattern_precedent: 1` rationale affirms the\n118\toperator already manages other components), so the +1 condition arguably\n119\tholds; the rationale conflates pipeline verification (no\n120\tarchitecture-context file) with codebase foundation; (b)\n121\t`open_questions: 1` (\"no open questions change this epic's approach\")\n122\twhile the epic's own scope requires confirming the Platform Operator's\n123\townership and extension surface with the owning team before starting —\n124\tan unresolved question that could change the approach; 0 would be more\n125\taccurate. Both are conservative (understate implementability) and\n126\trationale-backed, so they are arguable rather than rubric\n127\tcontradictions.\n128\t\n129\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n130\tEvery epic has testable ACs derived from the strategy. Rule-mandated\n131\tACs are present everywhere applicable: build-pipeline-green on the\n132\tkonflux epic (BRANCH-A-E004) and on the general implementation\n133\t(BRANCH-A-E005, with correct \"gates first execution, not this epic's\n134\t