{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-addec933964985f4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9007\n3\tepic_count: 11\n4\tcritical_path_length: 5\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\trevised: true\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9007 (Bring-your-own vector database for RAG workloads)\n11\t\n12\t## Triage\n13\t\n14\tNot below-threshold: the strategy spans multiple components (Llama Stack,\n15\tDashboard, Platform Operator), multiple teams, and contains a genuine unknown —\n16\tthe managed-vs-external posture decision (HLR-1, Open Question 1) — whose\n17\tanswer changes which downstream epics exist. Not docs-only: code changes are\n18\trequired in at least one posture. Full decomposition follows.\n19\t\n20\t## Decomposition Shape\n21\t\n22\tHLR-1 is a decision with exactly two bounded outcomes, and the strategy states\n23\texplicitly that the outcome \"forks the implementation structure for HLR-2\n24\tthrough HLR-5\". This is modeled as a conditional decomposition:\n25\t\n26\t- **Main plan**: one Investigation epic (E001) that resolves the posture.\n27\t- **Branch A** (`BRANCH-A-*`): platform-managed posture — operator-deployed\n28\t  Milvus with productized images. Milvus is not in the platform inventory\n29\t  (no architecture-context file), so Rule 20 generates the full onboarding\n30\t  chain (repo-onboarding + license-validation → konflux-onboarding, with the\n31\t  general implementation gated only by license-validation).\n32\t- **Branch B** (`BRANCH-B-*`): external-connection-only posture — per-project\n33\t  connection registration with validated connectivity.\n34\t\n35\tBranch epics are conditional alternatives attached to the gating\n36\tInvestigation; exactly one branch executes.\n37\t\n38\t## Epic List\n39\t\n40\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Component | Priority |\n41\t|----|-------|------|------|-----------|----------|\n42\t| E001 | Vector store posture decision: managed vs external-connection-only | Investigation | RHOAI GenAI | Llama Stack | P0 |\n43\t| BRANCH-A-E002 | Midstream repo onboarding for Milvus under opendatahub-io | Implementation | ODH Platform | Platform Operator | P0 |\n44\t| BRANCH-A-E003 | License validation for Milvus and transitive dependencies | Implementation | ODH Platform | Platform Operator | P0 |\n45\t| BRANCH-A-E004 | Konflux onboarding for the productized Milvus image build | Implementation | ODH Platform | Platform Operator | P0 |\n46\t| BRANCH-A-E005 | Platform Operator deployment and lifecycle for managed Milvus | Implementation | ODH Platform | Platform Operator | P0 |\n47\t| BRANCH-A-E006 | Llama Stack RAG provider integration for the managed vector store | Implementation | RHOAI GenAI | Llama Stack | P1 |\n48\t| BRANCH-A-E007 | Dashboard deploy-and-manage UI for the managed vector store | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | Dashboard | P1 |\n49\t| BRANCH-A-E008 | Documentation for the platform-managed vector store posture | Implementation | RHOAI Documentation | Documentation | P1 |\n50\t| BRANCH-B-E002 | External vector store connection management with validated connectivity | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | Dashboard | P0 |\n51\t| BRANCH-B-E003 | Llama Stack RAG provider integration for registered external vector stores | Implementation | RHOAI GenAI | Llama Stack | P1 |\n52\t| BRANCH-B-E004 | Documentation for the external-connection posture | Implementation | RHOAI Documentation | Documentation | P1 |\n53\t\n54\tNotes:\n55\t- **docs-authoring priority exception** (Step 4): both documentation epics take\n56\t  P1 from the strategy frontmatter `priority: Major` (Critical→P0,\n57\t  Major→P1), not from priority inheritance.\n58\t- **Branch B HLR consolidation**: HLR-2 (external path: \"data scientists can\n59\t  register an external vector store connection per project with validated\n60\t  connectivity\") and HLR-4 (external path: \"connection management UI\") describe\n61\t  the same connection-management surface for the same component (Dashboard)\n62\t  and team — HLR-4 is the UI presentation of HLR-2's capability. They are one\n63\t  epic (BRANCH-B-E002) covering both HLR ids at the higher priority (P0),\n64\t  per the redundant-HLR consolidation rule. In Branch A the two HLRs land on\n65\t  different components/teams (Platform Operator vs Dashboard), so they are\n66\t  separate epics by the component/team boundary rule, not by priority.\n67\t\n68\t## Dependency DAG\n69\t\n70\tBranch A and Branch B are mutually exclusive alternatives selected by E001.\n71\t\n72\t```mermaid\n73\tgraph TD\n74\t    E001[\"E001 Investigation: posture decision\"] --> AE002[\"A-E002 repo-onboarding\"]\n75\t    E001 --> AE003[\"A-E003 license-validation\"]\n76\t    E001 --> AE004[\"A-E004 konflux-onboarding\"]\n77\t    E001 --> AE005[\"A-E005 operator deployment\"]\n78\t    E001 --> BE002[\"B-E002 connection management\"]\n79\t    AE002 --> AE004\n80\t    AE003 --> AE005\n81\t    AE005 --> AE006[\"A-E006 Llama Stack provider\"]\n82\t    AE005 --> AE007[\"A-E007 Dashboard UI\"]\n83\t    AE002 --> AE008[\"A-E008 docs (managed)\"]\n84\t    AE003 --> AE008\n85\t    AE004 --> AE008\n86\t    AE005 --> AE008\n87\t    AE006 --> AE008\n88\t    AE007 --> AE008\n89\t    BE002 --> BE003[\"B-E003 Llama Stack provider\"]\n90\t    BE002 --> BE004[\"B-E004 docs (external)\"]\n91\t    BE003 --> BE004\n92\t```\n93\t\n94\t## DAG Justification\n95\t\n96\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n97\t|------|------|-----------|\n98\t| E001 → A-E002 | Rule 3 (Investigation gate) | Posture decision determines whether the Milvus onboarding chain exists at all; true gate, action=remove. |\n99\t| E001 → A-E003 | Rule 3 (Investigation gate) | Same gate; license scan only runs in the managed posture. |\n100\t| E001 → A-E004 | Rule 3 (Investigation gate) | Same gate; Konflux onboarding only needed for the productized image. |\n101\t| E001 → A-E005 | Rule 3 (Investigation gate) | Same gate; managed deployment does not exist in the external posture. |\n102\t| E001 → B-E002 | Rule 3 (Investigation gate) | Same gate; connection registration does not exist in the managed posture. |\n103\t| A-E002 → A-E004 | Rule 5 (repo-onboarding → konflux-onboarding serial) | The Konflux pipeline needs the midstream repo to exist. |\n104\t| A-E003 → A-E005 | Rule 9 (license-validation → general implementation serial) | If licenses fail, the dependency set changes and the approach is affected. |\n105\t| A-E004 ∥ A-E005 | Rule 10 (konflux ∥ general implementation, NO edge) | Config is independent of code; coupling is enforced by the \"build pipeline green\" AC on A-E005, never by a DAG edge. |\n106\t| A-E005 → A-E006 | Rule 12/13 (framework → consumer) | The Llama Stack provider integration builds against the operator-provisioned vector store capability and its configuration surface. |\n107\t| A-E005 → A-E007 | Rule 12 (framework → consumer) | The Dashboard UI builds against the operator CRs the deployment epic introduces; the Dashboard owns no data plane (architecture context). |\n108\t| all A-impl → A-E008 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring last) | Docs describe what was built; blocked by every Branch A Implementation epic. Edges do not trigger priority inheritance (docs-authoring exception). |\n109\t| B-E002 → B-E003 | Rule 12/13 (framework → consumer) | The Llama Stack provider integration builds against the connection registration capability and its data structure. |\n110\t| B-E002, B-E003 → B-E004 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring last) | Blocked by every Branch B Implementation epic. |\n111\t\n112\tNo edge between E001-gated branch A and branch B epics: the branches are\n113\tmutually exclusive alternatives, not a sequence.\n114\t\n115\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n116\t\n117\t| HLR | Priority | Main plan | Branch A (managed) | Branch B (external) |\n118\t|-----|----------|-----------|--------------------|---------------------|\n119\t| HLR-1 | P0 | E001 (decision + documented evaluation) | — (resolved by E001) | — (resolved by E001) |\n120\t| HLR-2 | P0 | — (conditional) | BRANCH-A-E005 (managed deploy via operator, productized images) | BRANCH-B-E002 (per-project connection registration, validated connectivity) |\n121\t| HLR-3 | P1 | — (conditional) | BRANCH-A-E006 | BRANCH-B-E003 |\n122\t| HLR-4 | P1 | — (conditional) | BRANCH-A-E007 (deploy-and-manage UI) | BRANCH-B-E002 (connection management UI — consolidated with HLR-2, same surface) |\n123\t| HLR-5 | P2 | — (conditional) | BRANCH-A-E008 | BRANCH-B-E004 |\n124\t\n125\tEvery HLR is covered by E001 plus exactly one branch; no orphaned\n126\trequirements. HLR-2 through HLR-5 are inherently conditional on HLR-1 per the\n127\tstrategy's own wording (\"Depending on that decision\"), which is why they have\n128\tno main-plan Implementation epic.\n129\t\n130\t## Conditional Branches\n131\t\n132\t- **Branch A — platform-managed (operator-deployed Milvus)**: epics\n133\t  BRANCH-A-E002 … BRANCH-A-E008. `gated_by` E001, `branch=A`,\n134\t  `gate_failure_impact.action=remove` — if the external-connection posture is\n135\t  chosen, none of this branch's epics run.\n136\t- **Branch B — external-connection-only**: epics BRANCH-B-E002 …\n137\t  BRANCH-B-E004. `gated_by` E001, `branch=B`, `gate_failure_impact.action=remove`\n138\t  — if the managed posture is chosen, none of this branch's epics run.\n139\t\n140\tBranch epics are excluded from the main-plan critical path. The main plan is\n141\tE001 alone (critical path length 1). Counting the longest branch chain\n142\t(E001 → A-E003 → A-E005 → A-E006/A-E007 → A-E008), the end-to-end critical\n143\tpath is 5 epics — the parallel A-E006/A-E007 siblings each contribute one\n144\tnode to the chain, not two; `critical_path_length` reports 5 and `epic_count`\n145\treports all 11 epics including branches.\n146\t\n147\t## Tiered Delivery\n148\t\n149\tNot applicable. There is no external dependency with uncertain timing: the\n150\tgating unknown is an internal product decision (E001), and the upstream\n151\tdependency in Branch A (Milvus) is an established OSS project with no\n152\tacceptance-gated upstream contribution. Tiering within a posture is a\n153\tscheduling decision for the implementing teams, not a structural split the\n154\tstrategy demands.\n155\t\n156\t## Health Warnings\n157\t\n158\t1. **Missing strategy sections**: the strategy has no Impacted Teams table, no\n159\t   Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then acceptance criteria, and no\n160\t   Non-Functional Requirements; the Affected Components section is a bare list\n161\t   without change/owner columns. Team assignments below are derived from\n162\t   architecture-context owning teams where available (Llama Stack → RHOAI\n163\t   GenAI, Dashboard → RHOAI Dashboard) and assumed elsewhere.\n164\t2. **Platform Operator is not in the platform inventory**: there is no\n165\t   architecture-context file for Platform Operator, so its existence,\n166\t   ownership, and extension surface are unverified by this pipeline. Team\n167\t   \"ODH Platform\" is an assumption (health warning, not an Investigation —\n168\t   the strategy names the Platform Operator as the delivery vehicle, and the\n169\t   posture decision in E001 is the genuine gate; if the managed posture is\n170\t   chosen, the implementing team should confirm operator ownership first).\n171\t3. **Milvus is not a canonical Jira component**: the canonical component list\n172\t   has no vector-database entry. All Milvus onboarding and operator-deployment\n173\t   epics (BRANCH-A-E002 … BRANCH-A-E005) are filed under the closest canonical\n174\t   component, `Platform Operator`, because the managed path delivers Milvus\n175\t   through it. Log this mapping if the component list later gains a\n176\t   vector-store entry.\n177\t4. **Scope trap (mild)**: \"shipping both postures in the same release\" is out\n178\t   of scope, so neither branch may accumulate the other posture's epics as\n179\t   \"nice to have\" — reviewers should reject scope creep across branches.\n180\t5. **Component mapping note**: BRANCH-B-E002 files the connection-registration\n181\t   backend and UI as one Dashboard epic; if the registration mechanism turns\n182\t   out to be owned by a different component/team than the Dashboard, that is\n183\t   an implementation-discovery outcome, not a decomposition error.\n184\t\n185\t## Ambiguity Flags\n186\t\n187\tNone beyond the health warnings above. The single genuine unknown (posture)\n188\tis explicit in the strategy and modeled as the gating Investigation with two\n189\tbounded branches.\n190\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-88d8c5852f699152","agent_id":"ab9e2677007724aa0","session_id":"456aa445-a015-4ed6-b66f-fb5c63ab7c74","uuid":"406c1e89-a3e7-46b7-87c5-db69da10978e","timestamp":"2026-10-22T17:59:55.334Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-addec933964985f4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9007 decomposition"}
