nfiguration model the Llama Stack distribution already\n51\t  supports.\n52\t- Resolve provider configuration from the project's registered connections\n53\t  rather than requiring hand-edited distribution config files.\n54\t- Verify the integration end to end with a RAG workload that stores and\n55\t  retrieves embeddings through a registered external vector store.\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- A Llama Stack distribution can be configured to use a project's registered\n60\t  external vector store connection as its RAG provider through supported\n61\t  configuration surfaces — no hand-editing of distribution config files.\n62\t- A RAG workload run against the distribution stores and retrieves embeddings\n63\t  through the registered external vector store successfully.\n64\t- Credentials from the registered connection are consumed through the\n65\t  platform's secret handling, not duplicated into distribution config files.\n66\t\n67\t## HLR Traceability\n68\t\n69\t- HLR-3 (P1): Llama Stack distributions can consume the chosen vector store\n70\t  as a RAG provider without hand-editing distribution configs — external\n71\t  path.\n72\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-88d8c5852f699152","agent_id":"ab9e2677007724aa0","session_id":"456aa445-a015-4ed6-b66f-fb5c63ab7c74","uuid":"90899c5d-e12a-4a3e-ac7f-d3067f2c224d","timestamp":"2026-10-22T18:00:15.770Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b76d8a1193a8a692","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9007 decomposition"}
