and identify which downstream implementation structure the\n48\t  decision selects (managed onboarding chain vs connection registration).\n49\t- Confirm feasibility inputs for the chosen posture only as needed to make the\n50\t  decision defensible (for example, whether a productized Milvus image is\n51\t  supportable in disconnected environments); this investigation does not\n52\t  implement either posture.\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- A written evaluation exists that compares platform-managed\n57\t  (operator-deployed Milvus) versus external-connection-only against\n58\t  supportability cost, disconnected-environment viability, and\n59\t  time-to-market, with the trade-offs for each criterion stated explicitly.\n60\t- A single posture decision is recorded with rationale that references the\n61\t  evaluation.\n62\t- The decision record states which downstream implementation structure\n63\t  applies, so implementation epics can be scheduled without re-litigating the\n64\t  decision.\n65\t\n66\t## HLR Traceability\n67\t\n68\t- HLR-1 (P0): a decision is reached, with a documented evaluation, on the\n69\t  first supported vector store posture.\n70\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b32aebbc0fc9bcf2","agent_id":"af8f91c729ee13d90","session_id":"456aa445-a015-4ed6-b66f-fb5c63ab7c74","uuid":"b0c3c63f-7928-472d-95cd-5f76d80145e3","timestamp":"2026-10-22T18:09:54.760Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8e4928cb48c9589e","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Final review of RHAISTRAT-9007"}
