{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a78e05a5aad3b144","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-A-E006\n3\ttitle: Llama Stack RAG provider integration for the managed vector store\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9007\n5\tcomponent: Llama Stack\n6\tteam: RHOAI GenAI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tbranch: A\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9007-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9007-E001\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-A-E005\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: remove\n16\t  fallback_approach: If the external-connection-only posture is selected, the Llama\n17\t    Stack integration targets registered external connections instead; this epic is\n18\t    removed in favor of the external-path provider integration.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 1\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n23\t  existing_foundation: 1\n24\t  open_questions: 0\n25\t  external_dependency: 0\n26\t  human_process_gates: 0\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: High\n32\tai_implementability_score: 6\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Llama Stack RAG provider integration for the managed vector store\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tThis epic wires the managed vector store into Llama Stack as a RAG provider,\n40\tso Llama Stack distributions running on the platform can use the\n41\toperator-deployed Milvus without anyone hand-editing distribution\n42\tconfiguration files. Llama Stack exposes a provider-plugin model for RAG\n43\tproviders, and its architecture context already lists Milvus/vector providers\n44\tas the expected backing for RAG workflows.\n45\t\n46\t## Scope\n47\t\n48\t- Integrate the managed vector store as the RAG (vector) provider for Llama\n49\t  Stack distributions on the platform, using the provider-plugin configuration\n50\t  model the Llama Stack distribution already supports.\n51\t- Make the provider configuration discoverable from the platform-side managed\n52\t  deployment (the operator-provisioned vector store instance) rather than\n53\t  requiring hand-edited distribution config files.\n54\t- Verify the integration end to end with a RAG workload that stores and\n55\t  retrieves embeddings through the managed vector store.\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- A Llama Stack distribution can be configured to use the managed vector\n60\t  store as its RAG provider through supported configuration surfaces — no\n61\t  hand-editing of distribution config files.\n62\t- A RAG workload run against the distribution stores and retrieves embeddings\n63\t  through the managed vector store successfully.\n64\t- The integration works against the operator-deployed instance without\n65\t  hard-coded connection details in the distribution configuration.\n66\t\n67\t## HLR Traceability\n68\t\n69\t- HLR-3 (P1): Llama Stack distributions can consume the chosen vector store\n70\t  as a RAG provider without hand-editing distribution configs.\n71\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b32aebbc0fc9bcf2","agent_id":"af8f91c729ee13d90","session_id":"456aa445-a015-4ed6-b66f-fb5c63ab7c74","uuid":"13183d4e-356a-4c10-8e15-33297d2acc43","timestamp":"2026-10-22T18:10:02.645Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a78e05a5aad3b144","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Final review of RHAISTRAT-9007"}
