{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8039ee69e7907005","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-B-E003\n3\ttitle: Llama Stack RAG provider integration for registered external vector stores\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9007\n5\tcomponent: Llama Stack\n6\tteam: RHOAI GenAI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tbranch: B\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9007-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9007-E001\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-B-E002\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: remove\n16\t  fallback_approach: If the platform-managed posture is selected, the Llama Stack\n17\t    integration targets the operator-provisioned vector store instead; this epic is\n18\t    removed in favor of the managed-path provider integration.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 1\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n23\t  existing_foundation: 1\n24\t  open_questions: 0\n25\t  external_dependency: 0\n26\t  human_process_gates: 0\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: High\n32\tai_implementability_score: 6\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Llama Stack RAG provider integration for registered external vector stores\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tThis epic wires registered external vector store connections into Llama\n40\tStack as RAG providers, so Llama Stack distributions on the platform can use\n41\ta project's registered external vector store without anyone hand-editing\n42\tdistribution configuration files. Llama Stack exposes a provider-plugin\n43\tmodel for RAG providers, and its architecture context lists Milvus/vector\n44\tproviders as the expected backing for RAG workflows.\n45\t\n46\t## Scope\n47\t\n48\t- Integrate registered external vector store connections as the RAG\n49\t  (vector) provider source for Llama Stack distributions, using the\n50\t  provider-plugin configuration model the Llama Stack distribution already\n51\t  supports.\n52\t- Resolve provider configuration from the project's registered connections\n53\t  rather than requiring hand-edited distribution config files.\n54\t- Verify the integration end to end with a RAG workload that stores and\n55\t  retrieves embeddings through a registered external vector store.\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- A Llama Stack distribution can be configured to use a project's registered\n60\t  external vector store connection as its RAG provider through supported\n61\t  configuration surfaces — no hand-editing of distribution config files.\n62\t- A RAG workload run against the distribution stores and retrieves embeddings\n63\t  through the registered external vector store successfully.\n64\t- Credentials from the registered connection are consumed through the\n65\t  platform's secret handling, not duplicated into distribution config files.\n66\t\n67\t## HLR Traceability\n68\t\n69\t- HLR-3 (P1): Llama Stack distributions can consume the chosen vector store\n70\t  as a RAG provider without hand-editing distribution configs — external\n71\t  path.\n72\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b32aebbc0fc9bcf2","agent_id":"af8f91c729ee13d90","session_id":"456aa445-a015-4ed6-b66f-fb5c63ab7c74","uuid":"97913c9e-4ecb-4fc9-8716-98bf3b3b6fa8","timestamp":"2026-10-22T18:10:10.231Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8039ee69e7907005","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Final review of RHAISTRAT-9007"}
